To build the module, ensure you have the following installed:
- libgretl
- python3-pybind11 package
- make framework (including pkg-config)
- a modern C++ compiler (LLVM/Clang++ and g++ have been tested)

To build the module, simply type 'make' in the top-level directory. If successful, you should get a file named 'gretl.cpython-3xx-x86_64-linux-gnu.so' on Linux (where 'xx' is the minor Python version number).


To test the module,
- either type 'make demoscript', or
- go to the 'demo' directory and type 'python3 demo.py'
In 'demo' directory you'll find another examples as well.
